IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap2-3val`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2015(e) to (n): students, aliens, the other bars and the State options (snap2).
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text; nothing here is verified against it.
-- JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- A function whose name says "is ineligible" answers JUST TRUE when the bar applies and JUST FALSE when the text says it does not.

§ `Section 2015(e): students`

DECLARE `s 2015(e) facts` HAS
    `the individual is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual's age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the individual is physically and mentally fit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is assigned to or placed in the institution through a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is part of a career and technical education program that may be completed in not more than 4 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is limited to remedial courses, basic adult education, literacy, or English as a second language` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is placed through a program under section 2296 of title 19` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is placed through another State or local government employment and training program, as determined to be appropriate by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the individual's hours of employment per week` IS A NUMBER
    `the individual participates in a State or federally financed work study program during the regular school year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the age of the dependent child in years` IS A NUMBER
    `adequate child care is available to enable the individual to attend class and satisfy the requirements of paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is enrolled as a result of participation in the work incentive program under title IV of the Social Security Act or its successor programs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is enrolled full-time as determined by the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual is a single parent` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:699 | No individual who is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this section shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of that or any other household if the individual is enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education, unless the individual—
-- src:700 | (1) is under age 18 or is age 50 or older;
-- src:701 | (2) is not physically or mentally fit;
-- src:702 | (3) is assigned to or placed in an institution of higher education through or in compliance with the requirements of—
-- src:703 | (A) a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act [29 U.S.C. 3111 et seq.];
-- src:704 | (B) an employment and training program under this section, subject to the condition that the course or program of study—
-- src:705 | (i) is part of a program of career and technical education (as defined in section 2302 of title 20) that may be completed in not more than 4 years at an institution of higher education (as defined in section 1002 of title 20); or
-- src:706 | (ii) is limited to remedial courses, basic adult education, literacy, or English as a second language;
-- src:707 | (C) a program under section 2296 of title 19; or
-- src:708 | (D) another program for the purpose of employment and training operated by a State or local government, as determined to be appropriate by the Secretary;
-- src:709 | (4) is employed a minimum of 20 hours per week or participating in a State or federally financed work study program during the regular school year;
-- src:710 | (5) is—
-- src:711 | (A) a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age 6; or
-- src:712 | (B) a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child above the age of 5 and under the age of 12 for whom adequate child care is not available to enable the individual to attend class and satisfy the requirements of paragraph (4);
-- src:713 | (6) is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.);
-- src:714 | (7) is so enrolled as a result of participation in the work incentive program under title IV of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] or its successor programs; or
-- src:715 | (8) is enrolled full-time in an institution of higher education, as determined by the institution, and is a single parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age 12.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(e) (src:699-715)
GIVEN f IS A `s 2015(e) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(e) the individual is ineligible as a student` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No individual who is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate"
        IF NOT f's `the individual is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the individual is enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT f's `the individual is enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the individual" is within one of items (1) to (8)
        IF `some exception` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): item (3)(D) turns on what the Secretary determines to be appropriate
        IF `some exception` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `some exception` MEANS
            `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds` (LIST `item (1)`, `item (2)`, `item (3)`, `item (4)`, `item (5)`, `item (6)`, `item (7)`, `item (8)`)
        -- (1) is under age 18 or is age 50 or older
        `item (1)` MEANS JUST (f's `the individual's age in years` LESS THAN 18 OR f's `the individual's age in years` AT LEAST 50)
        -- (2) is not physically or mentally fit
        `item (2)` MEANS JUST (NOT f's `the individual is physically and mentally fit`)
        -- (3) assigned to or placed in an institution of higher education through or in compliance with (A), (B)(i) or (ii), (C) or (D)
        `item (3)` MEANS
            `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds`
                (LIST JUST (f's `the individual is assigned to or placed in the institution through a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act`)
                    , JUST (f's `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is part of a career and technical education program that may be completed in not more than 4 years`)
                    , JUST (f's `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is limited to remedial courses, basic adult education, literacy, or English as a second language`)
                    , JUST (f's `the individual is placed through a program under section 2296 of title 19`)
                    , f's `the individual is placed through another State or local government employment and training program, as determined to be appropriate by the Secretary`)
        -- (4) employed a minimum of 20 hours per week or participating in a work study program during the regular school year
        `item (4)` MEANS JUST (f's `the individual's hours of employment per week` AT LEAST 20 OR f's `the individual participates in a State or federally financed work study program during the regular school year`)
        -- (5)(A) a parent with responsibility for a dependent child under age 6; (B) above the age of 5 and under the age of 12 for whom adequate child care is not available
        `item (5)` MEANS
            JUST (f's `the individual is a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child`
                  AND (f's `the age of the dependent child in years` LESS THAN 6
                       OR (f's `the age of the dependent child in years` GREATER THAN 5 AND f's `the age of the dependent child in years` LESS THAN 12 AND (NOT f's `adequate child care is available to enable the individual to attend class and satisfy the requirements of paragraph (4)`))))
        -- (6) receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV; (7) enrolled as a result of the work incentive program
        `item (6)` MEANS JUST (f's `the individual is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act`)
        `item (7)` MEANS JUST (f's `the individual is enrolled as a result of participation in the work incentive program under title IV of the Social Security Act or its successor programs`)
        -- (8) enrolled full-time as determined by the institution, and a single parent with responsibility for a dependent child under age 12
        `item (8)` MEANS
            JUST (f's `the individual is enrolled full-time as determined by the institution` AND f's `the individual is a single parent`
                  AND f's `the individual is a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child` AND f's `the age of the dependent child in years` LESS THAN 12)

§ `Section 2015(f): aliens`

-- src:717 | No individual who is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this section shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of that or any other household unless he or she is—
-- src:718 | (1) a resident of the United States; and
-- src:719 | (2) either—
-- src:720 | (A) a citizen or national of the United States;
-- src:721 | (B) an alien lawfully admitted for permanent residence as an immigrant as defined by sections 1101(a)(15) and 1101(a)(20) of title 8, excluding, among others, alien visitors, tourists, diplomats, and students who enter the United States temporarily with no intention of abandoning their residence in a foreign country;
-- src:722 | (C) an alien who has been granted the status of Cuban and Haitian entrant, as defined in section 501(e) of the Refugee Education Assistance Act of 1980 (Public Law 96–422); or
-- src:723 | (D) an individual who lawfully resides in the United States in accordance with a Compact of Free Association referred to in section 1612(b)(2)(G) of title 8.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(f) (src:717-723)
GIVEN person IS AN Individual
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(f) the individual is ineligible for want of residence or status` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she is— (1) a resident of the United States; and (2) either— (A) a citizen or national ...; (B) an alien lawfully admitted for permanent residence ...; (C) ... Cuban and Haitian entrant ...; or (D) ... a Compact of Free Association"
        IF person's `resident of the United States` AND `has one of the four statuses` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `has one of the four statuses` MEANS
            CONSIDER person's `immigration status`
            WHEN `a citizen or national of the United States` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an alien lawfully admitted for permanent residence` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a Cuban or Haitian entrant` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a resident under a Compact of Free Association` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `any other status` THEN FALSE

-- src:724 | The income (less, at State option, a pro rata share) and financial resources of the individual rendered ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this subsection shall be considered in determining the eligibility and the value of the allotment of the household of which such individual is a member.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(f), closing paragraph (src:724-724)
GIVEN `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the State has chosen to leave out a pro rata share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pro rata share, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2015(f) the income of the ineligible individual counted for the household, in dollars` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The income ... of the individual rendered ineligible to participate ... under this subsection"
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection` THEN NOTHING
        -- "The income (less, at State option, a pro rata share) ... shall be considered in determining the eligibility and the value of the allotment of the household"
        IF `the State has chosen to leave out a pro rata share` THEN JUST (`the individual's income, in dollars` MINUS `the pro rata share, in dollars`)
        OTHERWISE JUST `the individual's income, in dollars`

-- src:724 | The income (less, at State option, a pro rata share) and financial resources of the individual rendered ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this subsection shall be considered in determining the eligibility and the value of the allotment of the household of which such individual is a member.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(f), closing paragraph (src:724-724)
GIVEN `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(f) the financial resources of the ineligible individual are considered for the household` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The income ... and financial resources of the individual rendered ineligible to participate ... under this subsection"
    IF `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2015(g) to (j): State supplementary payments, transfers, comparable treatment, multiple benefits`

-- src:726 | No individual who receives supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.], State supplementary payments described in section 1616 of such Act [42 U.S.C. 1382e], or payments of the type referred to in section 212(a) of Public Law 93–66, as amended, shall be considered to be a member of a household for any month, if, for such month, such individual resides in a State which provides State supplementary payments (1) of the type described in section 1616(a) of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1382e(a)] and section 212(a) of Public Law 93–66, and (2) the level of which has been found by the Commissioner of Social Security to have been specifically increased so as to include the bonus value of food stamps.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(g) (src:726-726)
GIVEN `the individual receives supplemental security income benefits, State supplementary payments described in section 1616, or payments of the type referred to in section 212(a) of Public Law 93-66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual resides in a State that provides State supplementary payments of the type described in section 1616(a) and section 212(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner of Social Security has found the level specifically increased so as to include the bonus value of food stamps` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(g) the individual is not considered a member of a household for the month` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No individual who receives supplemental security income benefits ..., State supplementary payments ..., or payments of the type referred to in section 212(a)"
        IF NOT `the individual receives supplemental security income benefits, State supplementary payments described in section 1616, or payments of the type referred to in section 212(a) of Public Law 93-66` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, for such month, such individual resides in a State which provides State supplementary payments (1) of the type described" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT `the individual resides in a State that provides State supplementary payments of the type described in section 1616(a) and section 212(a)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the finding of the Commissioner of Social Security under (2) is an input
        OTHERWISE `the Commissioner of Social Security has found the level specifically increased so as to include the bonus value of food stamps`

DECLARE `s 2015(h) outcome` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(h) not ineligible under this subsection`
    `s 2015(h) ineligible for a period of up to one year from the date of discovery, ending` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `s 2015(h) not covered`

-- src:728 | No household that knowingly transfers assets for the purpose of qualifying or attempting to qualify for the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be eligible to participate in the program for a period of up to one year from the date of discovery of the transfer.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(h) (src:728-728)
GIVEN `the household knowingly transferred assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer was for the purpose of qualifying or attempting to qualify for the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of discovery of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the number of months for which the household is made ineligible` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 2015(h) outcome`
`s 2015(h) the household is ineligible on the date` MEANS
    -- MONTH ARITHMETIC (fork F-mo, NOTES): "a period of up to one year from the date of discovery" is computed with `add months`, which CLAMPS the day to the last day of a shorter month (31 January 2026 plus 1 month is 28 February 2026). The text does not say how a month is counted when the later month lacks the day; the other readings are "not covered" and rolling forward to 3 March.
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No household that knowingly transfers assets for the purpose of qualifying or attempting to qualify" (reading (a): a failed condition)
        IF NOT (`the household knowingly transferred assets` AND `the transfer was for the purpose of qualifying or attempting to qualify for the program`) THEN `s 2015(h) not ineligible under this subsection`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a period of up to one year"; a longer period, or none, is not described, and the text does not say who fixes the period
        IF `the number of months for which the household is made ineligible` GREATER THAN 12 OR `the number of months for which the household is made ineligible` LESS THAN 0 THEN `s 2015(h) not covered`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "from the date of discovery of the transfer" (before it, or after the period, the household is not ineligible under this subsection)
        IF `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the date of discovery of the transfer` OR `the date asked about` AT LEAST `add months` `the date of discovery of the transfer` `the number of months for which the household is made ineligible` THEN `s 2015(h) not ineligible under this subsection`
        OTHERWISE `s 2015(h) ineligible for a period of up to one year from the date of discovery, ending` ((`add months` `the date of discovery of the transfer` `the number of months for which the household is made ineligible`) MINUS 1)

-- src:730 | (1) In general
-- src:731 | If a disqualification is imposed on a member of a household for a failure of the member to perform an action required under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program, the State agency may impose the same disqualification on the member of the household under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(i)(1) (src:730-731)
GIVEN `a disqualification is imposed on a member of a household for a failure to perform an action required under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(i)(1) the State agency may impose the same disqualification under the program` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a disqualification is imposed on a member of a household for a failure of the member to perform an action required under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program"
    IF `a disqualification is imposed on a member of a household for a failure to perform an action required under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:732 | (2) Rules and procedures
-- src:733 | If a disqualification is imposed under paragraph (1) for a failure of an individual to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), the State agency may use the rules and procedures that apply under part A of title IV of the Act to impose the same disqualification under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(i)(2) (src:732-733)
GIVEN `the disqualification is imposed under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(i)(2) the State agency may use the rules and procedures of part A of title IV` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a disqualification is imposed under paragraph (1) for a failure of an individual to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act"
    IF `the disqualification is imposed under paragraph (1)` AND `the failure was to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:734 | (3) Application after disqualification period
-- src:735 | A member of a household disqualified under paragraph (1) may, after the disqualification period has expired, apply for benefits under this chapter and shall be treated as a new applicant, except that a prior disqualification under subsection (d) shall be considered in determining eligibility.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(i)(3) (src:734-735)
GIVEN `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disqualification period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was a prior disqualification under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(i)(3) a prior disqualification under subsection (d) is considered in determining the former member's eligibility` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member of a household disqualified under paragraph (1) may, after the disqualification period has expired, apply for benefits"
    IF `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` AND `the disqualification period has expired` AND `there was a prior disqualification under subsection (d)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:734 | (3) Application after disqualification period
-- src:735 | A member of a household disqualified under paragraph (1) may, after the disqualification period has expired, apply for benefits under this chapter and shall be treated as a new applicant, except that a prior disqualification under subsection (d) shall be considered in determining eligibility.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(i)(3) (src:734-735)
GIVEN `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disqualification period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(i)(3) the member who applies is treated as a new applicant` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, after the disqualification period has expired, apply for benefits under this chapter and shall be treated as a new applicant"
    IF `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` AND `the disqualification period has expired` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2015(j) outcome` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(j) not ineligible under this subsection`
    `s 2015(j) ineligible for a period` HAS `the period` IS A `Period of ineligibility`

-- src:737 | An individual shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of any household for a 10-year period if the individual is found by a State agency to have made, or is convicted in a Federal or State court of having made, a fraudulent statement or representation with respect to the identity or place of residence of the individual in order to receive multiple benefits simultaneously under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(j) (src:737-737)
GIVEN `the individual is found by a State agency to have made a fraudulent statement or representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is convicted in a Federal or State court of having made a fraudulent statement or representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement or representation was with respect to the identity or place of residence of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in order to receive multiple benefits simultaneously under the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 2015(j) outcome`
`s 2015(j) the period of ineligibility for receiving multiple benefits` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be ineligible ... for a 10-year period if the individual is found by a State agency to have made, or is convicted ... of having made, a fraudulent statement or representation with respect to the identity or place of residence of the individual in order to receive multiple benefits simultaneously" (reading (a): a failed "if")
    -- the text does not say from when the 10-year period runs (see the fork register)
    IF (`the individual is found by a State agency to have made a fraudulent statement or representation` OR `the individual is convicted in a Federal or State court of having made a fraudulent statement or representation`)
       AND `the statement or representation was with respect to the identity or place of residence of the individual`
       AND `it was made in order to receive multiple benefits simultaneously under the program`
        THEN `s 2015(j) ineligible for a period` (`for a number of years` 10)
        ELSE `s 2015(j) not ineligible under this subsection`

§ `Section 2015(k): fleeing felons`

-- src:740 | No member of a household who is otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be eligible to participate in the program as a member of that or any other household during any period during which the individual is—
-- src:741 | (A) fleeing to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, under the law of the place from which the individual is fleeing, for a crime, or attempt to commit a crime, that is a felony under the law of the place from which the individual is fleeing or that, in the case of New Jersey, is a high misdemeanor under the law of New Jersey; or
-- src:742 | (B) violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under a Federal or State law.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(k)(1) (src:740-742)
GIVEN `the person is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is fleeing, as the Secretary defines the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the flight is to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a felony under the law of the place fled from, or for a high misdemeanor in New Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under a Federal or State law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(k)(1) the individual is ineligible while fleeing or violating probation or parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No member of a household who is otherwise eligible to participate"
        IF NOT `the person is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate` THEN NOTHING
        -- clause (B): "violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under a Federal or State law"
        IF `the individual is violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under a Federal or State law` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- clause (A): "fleeing to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction ... for a crime ... that is a felony"
        IF `the flight is to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a felony under the law of the place fled from, or for a high misdemeanor in New Jersey` THEN `the individual is fleeing, as the Secretary defines the term`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during any period during which the individual is" fleeing for a felony or violating probation or parole (reading (a): a failed condition)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:745 | (A) define the terms “fleeing” and “actively seeking” for purposes of this subsection; and
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(k)(2)(A) (src:745-745)
GIVEN `the Secretary's definition covers the individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(k)(2)(A) the individual is fleeing or actively sought, as the Secretary defines the terms` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "The Secretary shall— (A) define the terms “fleeing” and “actively seeking” for purposes of this subsection"; with no definition supplied the answer is NOTHING
    `the Secretary's definition covers the individual`

-- src:746 | (B) ensure that State agencies use consistent procedures established by the Secretary that disqualify individuals whom law enforcement authorities are actively seeking for the purpose of holding criminal proceedings against the individual.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(k)(2)(B) (src:746-746)
GIVEN `law enforcement authorities are actively seeking the individual for the purpose of holding criminal proceedings against the individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(k)(2)(B) the State agency is to disqualify the individual under the Secretary's consistent procedures` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "individuals whom law enforcement authorities are actively seeking for the purpose of holding criminal proceedings against the individual"
    IF `law enforcement authorities are actively seeking the individual for the purpose of holding criminal proceedings against the individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2015(l) to (n): child support`

-- src:749 | At the option of a State agency, subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), no natural or adoptive parent or other individual (collectively referred to in this subsection as “the individual”) who is living with and exercising parental control over a child under the age of 18 who has an absent parent shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless the individual cooperates with the State agency administering the program established under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 651 et seq.)—
-- src:750 | (A) in establishing the paternity of the child (if the child is born out of wedlock); and
-- src:751 | (B) in obtaining support for—
-- src:752 | (i) the child; or
-- src:753 | (ii) the individual and the child.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(l)(1) (src:749-753)
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a parent or other individual living with and exercising parental control over a child under the age of 18 who has an absent parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child was born out of wedlock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual cooperates in establishing the paternity of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual cooperates in obtaining support for the child, or for the individual and the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(l) the individual is ineligible for want of cooperation with the child support agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the option of a State agency", and only for an individual "living with and exercising parental control over a child under the age of 18 who has an absent parent"
        IF NOT `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the individual is a parent or other individual living with and exercising parental control over a child under the age of 18 who has an absent parent` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the individual cooperates ... (A) in establishing the paternity of the child (if the child is born out of wedlock); and (B) in obtaining support"
        IF `the individual cooperates in obtaining support for the child, or for the individual and the child` AND (`the individual cooperates in establishing the paternity of the child` OR (NOT `the child was born out of wedlock`)) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) shall not apply to the individual if good cause is found for refusing to cooperate" (paragraph (2), in `s 2015(l)(2) ...`)
        IF `s 2015(l)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the individual` `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): good cause is for the State agency to find under the Secretary's standards, and none was supplied
        IF `s 2015(l)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the individual` `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:754 | (2) Good cause for noncooperation
-- src:755 | Paragraph (1) shall not apply to the individual if good cause is found for refusing to cooperate, as determined by the State agency in accordance with standards prescribed by the Secretary in consultation with the Secretary of Health and Human Services. The standards shall take into consideration circumstances under which cooperation may be against the best interests of the child.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(l)(2) (src:754-755)
GIVEN `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(l)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) shall not apply to the individual if good cause is found for refusing to cooperate" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): good cause is "as determined by the State agency in accordance with standards prescribed by the Secretary"; no finding was supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:756 | (3) Fees
-- src:757 | Paragraph (1) shall not require the payment of a fee or other cost for services provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 651 et seq.).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(l)(3) (src:756-757)
GIVEN `the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(l)(3) the individual is required to pay a fee or other cost for the service` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) shall not require the payment of a fee or other cost for services provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the clause speaks only of "services provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act"
    IF `the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:759 | (1) In general
-- src:760 | At the option of a State agency, subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), a putative or identified noncustodial parent of a child under the age of 18 (referred to in this subsection as “the individual”) shall not be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the individual refuses to cooperate with the State agency administering the program established under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 651 et seq.)—
-- src:761 | (A) in establishing the paternity of the child (if the child is born out of wedlock); and
-- src:762 | (B) in providing support for the child.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(m)(1) (src:759-762)
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a putative or identified noncustodial parent of a child under the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child was born out of wedlock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual refuses to cooperate in establishing the paternity of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual refuses to cooperate in providing support for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(m)(1) the noncustodial parent is ineligible for refusing to cooperate with the child support agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the option of a State agency", and only for "a putative or identified noncustodial parent of a child under the age of 18"
        IF NOT `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the individual is a putative or identified noncustodial parent of a child under the age of 18` THEN NOTHING
        -- the two limbs are joined by "and": the reading taken needs refusal as to both, paternity counting only "if the child is born out of wedlock" (see the fork register)
        IF `the individual refuses to cooperate in providing support for the child` AND (`the individual refuses to cooperate in establishing the paternity of the child` OR (NOT `the child was born out of wedlock`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be eligible ... if the individual refuses to cooperate" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:763 | (2) Refusal to cooperate
-- src:764 | (A) Guidelines
-- src:765 | The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Health and Human Services, shall develop guidelines on what constitutes a refusal to cooperate under paragraph (1).
-- src:766 | (B) Procedures
-- src:767 | The State agency shall develop procedures, using guidelines developed under subparagraph (A), for determining whether an individual is refusing to cooperate under paragraph (1).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(m)(2) (src:763-767)
GIVEN `the Secretary's guidelines and the State agency's procedures say the matter is a refusal to cooperate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(m)(2) the matter is a refusal to cooperate under the guidelines and procedures` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Health and Human Services, shall develop guidelines on what constitutes a refusal to cooperate" and the State agency "shall develop procedures"; what they say is not in the text, so with none supplied the answer is NOTHING
    `the Secretary's guidelines and the State agency's procedures say the matter is a refusal to cooperate`

